<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Loading a URDF lets you specify collision shapes, mass, inertia, constraints etc.<br><br>It is work-in-progress, there is not much documentation for the new API yet, I would suggest try getting pybullet to run and give some feedback.<br>There are a few scripts in Bullet/examples/pybullet. <br><br>There will also be C++ access, using Bullet\examples\RoboticsLearning\b3RobotSimAPI.h. Once this is more complete, it will be rename b3PhysicsSimAPI.h...<br>You will be able to do your own graphics engine of course, and use the Bullet connect 'DIRECT' method (instead of GUI or SHARED_MEMORY).</div></blockquote>Ok, first attempt to get pybullet to be built on Linux Mint 17.3, x64 , GCC 4.8.4, Python 3.5.1....<br>got a linker error, see below<br><br>and CFLAGS / CCFLAGS / CPPFLAGS = '-fPIC' before the premake4_linux64 or make command didnt have an effect<br><br>Input:<br><br>CPPFLAGS='-fPIC' ./premake4_linux64 --enable_pybullet --python_include_dir="/home/martin/BlenderSVN/build/bin/2.78/python/include/python3.5m" <br>--python_lib_dir="/home/martin/BlenderSVN/build/bin/2.78/python/lib/python3.5" gmake<br><br>and make in the gmake dir<br><br>Output...(snip)<br><br>...<br>==== Building BulletFileLoader (release64) ====<br>==== Building BulletWorldImporter (release64) ====<br>==== Building pybullet (release64) ====<br>Linking pybullet<br>/usr/bin/ld: ../../bin/libBulletExampleBrowserLib_gmake_x64_release.a(OpenGLExampleBrowser.o): relocation R_X86_64_32 against `.rodata.str1.1' can not be used when making a shared object; recompile with -fPIC<br>../../bin/libBulletExampleBrowserLib_gmake_x64_release.a: error adding symbols: Bad value<br>collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status<br>make[1]: *** [../../bin/libpybullet_gmake_x64_release.so] Error 1<br>make: *** [pybullet] Error 2<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9237">scorpion81</a> — Sat Oct 15, 2016 5:05 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
