Loading a URDF lets you specify collision shapes, mass, inertia, constraints etc.<br><br>It is work-in-progress, there is not much documentation for the new API yet, I would suggest try getting pybullet to run and give some feedback.<br>There are a few scripts in Bullet/examples/pybullet. <br><br>There will also be C++ access, using Bullet\examples\RoboticsLearning\b3RobotSimAPI.h. Once this is more complete, it will be rename b3PhysicsSimAPI.h...<br>You will be able to do your own graphics engine of course, and use the Bullet connect 'DIRECT' method (instead of GUI or SHARED_MEMORY).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sat Oct 15, 2016 3:56 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
