<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Another question... since the pybullet wrapper seems not exactly what i can use for the purpose of operating bullet via python</div></blockquote>Why not?<br><br>pybullet and the underlying shared memory C-API will be the new Bullet 3.x API. I plan to create a backend so you can automatically select Bullet 2.x or Bullet 3.x (or other physics engines) under the hood. Those Bullet 3.x bindings will start happenening around PhysicsServerCommandProcessor.cpp...</div></blockquote>Ah ok, well i guess i did not understand yet how this new shared memory C-API works. Like... which commands in particular are necessary to replicate the basic HelloWorld example from the (old) wiki ?<br>Like building a world, adding rigidbodies, setting shapes, adding constraints ?<br>Is there some documentation i might have overlooked ?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9237">scorpion81</a> — Sat Oct 15, 2016 3:42 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
